1
00:02:31,017 --> 00:02:36,017
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:36,017 --> 00:02:41,017
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:41,017 --> 00:02:45,017
the legendary treasure left behind by Gold Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:45,017 --> 00:02:50,017
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum gum fruit,

5
00:02:50,017 --> 00:02:53,017
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:53,017 --> 00:02:56,017
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,017 --> 00:02:59,017
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,017 --> 00:03:02,017
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:03,017 --> 00:03:05,017
Now this is exciting!

10
00:03:06,017 --> 00:03:09,017
I can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:09,017 --> 00:03:12,017
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:12,017 --> 00:03:17,017
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,017 --> 00:03:23,017
Separated from the rest of the Straw Hat crew,

14
00:03:23,017 --> 00:03:28,017
Luffy is headed to Navy Headquarters to rescue his brother Ace from execution.

15
00:03:29,017 --> 00:03:35,017
It's him.

16
00:03:35,017 --> 00:03:36,017
It's him.

17
00:03:39,017 --> 00:03:43,017
You figure. It's a surprise attack. Whitebeard is no fool.

18
00:03:43,017 --> 00:03:45,017
Oh, don't act like you're so smart.

19
00:03:48,017 --> 00:03:50,017
There's a shadow in the middle of the bay!

20
00:03:50,017 --> 00:03:54,017
It's just as I feared. Why didn't we plan for this?

21
00:03:54,017 --> 00:03:57,017
They got their ships coated to ambushes from underwater!

22
00:03:57,017 --> 00:03:58,017
They got their ships coated to ambushes from underwater!

23
00:04:09,017 --> 00:04:11,017
It's Whitebeard's ship, the Moby Dick!

24
00:04:11,017 --> 00:04:28,017
The beginning of the war! Ace Whitebeard's past!

25
00:04:28,017 --> 00:04:29,017
It's past!

26
00:04:41,017 --> 00:04:43,017
Seriously? There are even more?

27
00:04:43,017 --> 00:04:48,017
They're still surfacing three more Whitebeard Pirate ships!

28
00:04:48,017 --> 00:04:49,017
They've infiltrated the bay!

29
00:04:49,017 --> 00:04:54,017
Oh, holy crap! It's First Division Commander Marco!

30
00:04:54,017 --> 00:04:58,017
I'm counting 14 commanders! They're all here!

31
00:04:58,017 --> 00:04:59,017
I'm counting 14 commanders! They're all here!

32
00:04:59,017 --> 00:05:03,017
I'm counting 14 commanders! They're all here!

33
00:05:03,017 --> 00:05:09,017
Oh, my God!

34
00:05:09,017 --> 00:05:12,017
I'm counting 14 commanders! They're all here!

35
00:05:13,017 --> 00:05:15,017
Oh, my God!

36
00:05:15,017 --> 00:05:16,017
Oh, my God!

37
00:05:16,017 --> 00:05:18,017
Oh, my God!

38
00:05:18,017 --> 00:05:20,017
Oh, my God!

39
00:05:20,017 --> 00:05:23,017
Oh, my God!

40
00:05:23,017 --> 00:05:26,017
Oh, my God!

41
00:05:26,017 --> 00:05:27,017
Oh, my God!

42
00:05:27,017 --> 00:05:29,017
Oh, my God!

43
00:05:29,017 --> 00:05:30,017
Oh, my God!

44
00:05:30,017 --> 00:05:57,257
It's been quite some time, Sengoku.

45
00:05:57,257 --> 00:05:59,177
Whitebeard.

46
00:06:00,017 --> 00:06:07,017
We've got plenty to talk about, like you not killing my son.

47
00:06:17,017 --> 00:06:20,017
I can't believe we let them get this close.

48
00:06:26,017 --> 00:06:28,017
Well, we're through the gate.

49
00:06:28,017 --> 00:06:32,017
Now, I'm just worried your dear old dad is gonna make an appearance.

50
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:34,017
I'm sure those government boys would love that.

51
00:06:34,017 --> 00:06:35,017
Dad?

52
00:06:35,017 --> 00:06:38,017
Dragon's not the type to sit back while his son's killed.

53
00:06:38,017 --> 00:06:40,017
When he's on a tear, things get nasty.

54
00:06:40,017 --> 00:06:41,017
Okay.

55
00:06:41,017 --> 00:06:43,017
Now, me and Ace, we don't have the same dad.

56
00:06:43,017 --> 00:06:44,017
Huh?

57
00:06:44,017 --> 00:06:47,017
You're right about Dragon being my dad, but not Ace.

58
00:06:47,017 --> 00:06:49,017
His dad is Gold Roger.

59
00:06:49,017 --> 00:06:50,017
Huh?

60
00:06:50,017 --> 00:06:51,017
Huh?

61
00:06:51,017 --> 00:06:53,017
Yeah, pretty cool, huh?

62
00:06:53,017 --> 00:06:56,017
It's a real shame you never got to meet him.

63
00:06:56,017 --> 00:06:58,017
He'd always get mad when I talked about it.

64
00:06:58,017 --> 00:06:59,017
Huh?

65
00:06:59,017 --> 00:07:00,017
Oh!

66
00:07:00,017 --> 00:07:01,017
That's supposed to be a secret.

67
00:07:01,017 --> 00:07:02,017
Ah!

68
00:07:02,017 --> 00:07:03,017
Ah!

69
00:07:03,017 --> 00:07:04,017
Ah!

70
00:07:04,017 --> 00:07:18,017
Sit tight for a second, Ace.

71
00:07:18,017 --> 00:07:32,157
The

72
00:07:32,157 --> 00:07:48,217
What did he do?

73
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:49,857
Did he crack the air?

74
00:07:49,857 --> 00:08:02,857
It looks like he set up a bomb.

75
00:08:02,857 --> 00:08:05,857
Maybe so, but the water level's too high.

76
00:08:05,857 --> 00:08:06,857
A secret!

77
00:08:06,857 --> 00:08:09,857
He's turning the ocean waters against us!

78
00:08:09,857 --> 00:08:11,857
The other side too!

79
00:08:11,857 --> 00:08:14,857
I knew Whitebeard was strong, but not like this.

80
00:08:19,857 --> 00:08:33,857
I'm finally heading out!

81
00:08:37,857 --> 00:08:39,857
Kick some bodies! Take care!

82
00:08:39,857 --> 00:08:42,857
Yeah! You got it! See ya!

83
00:08:42,857 --> 00:08:47,857
In three years! The next time you and me see each other, I'll be way stronger than you!

84
00:08:47,857 --> 00:08:48,857
Sure!

85
00:08:49,857 --> 00:08:52,857
BYE!

86
00:09:01,857 --> 00:09:04,857
It's about time we show him how it's done!

87
00:09:05,857 --> 00:09:08,857
That brat! I can't believe he became a pirate!

88
00:09:08,857 --> 00:09:12,857
It's a pirate ship! I've never seen their flag!

89
00:09:12,857 --> 00:09:22,857
He may be new, but he's not wasting any time in gaining notoriety.

90
00:09:22,857 --> 00:09:24,857
D, where is he from?

91
00:09:24,857 --> 00:09:27,857
We haven't been able to figure that out just yet.

92
00:09:27,857 --> 00:09:31,857
But he's clearly got the power of a Logia.

93
00:09:31,857 --> 00:09:36,857
Didn't expect the terror of the Grand Line to be such a dashing young fellow.

94
00:09:36,857 --> 00:09:39,857
Here they offered him a warlord position, but he refused.

95
00:09:39,857 --> 00:09:43,857
How long have these boys been at this? They're practically children.

96
00:09:44,857 --> 00:09:46,857
They're rushing like there's no tomorrow.

97
00:09:46,857 --> 00:09:49,857
You sure you want to do this, Captain?

98
00:09:49,857 --> 00:09:55,857
It's too late to complain now. I've got to see red-haired shanks.

99
00:09:55,857 --> 00:09:57,857
Spade pirates, huh?

100
00:09:57,857 --> 00:10:00,857
So you're the rookie everyone's talking about.

101
00:10:00,857 --> 00:10:02,857
Came to say hello.

102
00:10:02,857 --> 00:10:05,857
Wait, it's not what you're thinking.

103
00:10:05,857 --> 00:10:09,857
My little brother used to go on and on about you saving his life when he was young.

104
00:10:09,857 --> 00:10:11,857
So I'm here to say thank you.

105
00:10:11,857 --> 00:10:12,857
Luffy.

106
00:10:12,857 --> 00:10:15,857
Hot damn. I didn't know he had a brother.

107
00:10:15,857 --> 00:10:18,857
Well, come on in. I'm glad to meet you.

108
00:10:18,857 --> 00:10:20,857
Pop a squat and let's talk.

109
00:10:21,857 --> 00:10:23,857
This calls for a banquet.

110
00:10:27,857 --> 00:10:31,857
Oh yeah? Huh. He's still dead set on becoming King of the Pirates, huh?

111
00:10:31,857 --> 00:10:33,857
Pretty much all he ever talks about.

112
00:10:33,857 --> 00:10:38,857
Although, I feel bad for the kid.

113
00:10:38,857 --> 00:10:41,857
Cause I'm the one who's gonna be the next king.

114
00:10:41,857 --> 00:10:43,857
Yeah? You think so, huh?

115
00:10:43,857 --> 00:10:47,857
Well, the first thing I've got to do is let the whole world know that I mean business.

116
00:10:47,857 --> 00:10:50,857
I see. And what's your plan?

117
00:10:50,857 --> 00:10:54,857
I'm gonna defeat the most powerful man in the world, of course.

118
00:10:54,857 --> 00:10:56,857
So Whitebeard, then.

119
00:10:58,857 --> 00:11:02,857
Hey, big guy. I bet you can put me in touch with Whitebeard.

120
00:11:02,857 --> 00:11:05,857
You might be right, but you'd still lose that bet.

121
00:11:05,857 --> 00:11:07,857
Maybe I could introduce you, but I won't.

122
00:11:07,857 --> 00:11:09,857
Captain, do you realize that's Jinbei?

123
00:11:09,857 --> 00:11:12,857
Oh yeah? The Warlord.

124
00:11:12,857 --> 00:11:15,857
Beating him might bring us some prestige, then.

125
00:11:15,857 --> 00:11:18,857
I'm my own pirate. I'm not part of Whitebeard's crew.

126
00:11:18,857 --> 00:11:21,857
But I owe him one, so let's see what you got.

127
00:11:32,857 --> 00:11:36,857
There. How long have they been plating? Five days?

128
00:11:36,857 --> 00:11:38,857
You're both gonna die. Knock it off!

129
00:11:38,857 --> 00:12:03,857
What the hell is that?

130
00:12:03,857 --> 00:12:08,157
I heard one of you boys has made it your life's mission to see me dead.

131
00:12:11,157 --> 00:12:12,457
You wanna fight?

132
00:12:12,957 --> 00:12:14,957
I'm here to grant your wish.

133
00:12:16,457 --> 00:12:18,457
It's the white man pirates!

134
00:12:19,757 --> 00:12:22,257
One of me is enough for all of you.

135
00:12:33,857 --> 00:12:34,357
Huh?

136
00:12:34,357 --> 00:12:35,857
Blaze Band!

137
00:12:37,657 --> 00:12:38,357
Captain!

138
00:12:38,357 --> 00:12:39,357
Captain Ace!

139
00:12:39,357 --> 00:12:40,357
What are you doing?

140
00:12:40,357 --> 00:12:41,357
Get out of here!

141
00:12:41,357 --> 00:12:42,357
Run, now!

142
00:12:42,357 --> 00:12:43,857
Captain, no!

143
00:12:45,857 --> 00:12:47,057
What's the matter?

144
00:12:47,057 --> 00:12:49,357
Don't tell me you're getting cold feet.

145
00:12:49,357 --> 00:12:51,657
My crew's not trying to kill you.

146
00:12:51,657 --> 00:12:53,057
That's all me.

147
00:12:53,057 --> 00:12:54,357
You let them go!

148
00:12:55,057 --> 00:12:56,857
Giving me orders?

149
00:12:56,857 --> 00:12:58,357
You cocky punk.

150
00:13:04,357 --> 00:13:06,957
Monster Noir

151
00:13:12,957 --> 00:13:14,157
ava

152
00:13:14,757 --> 00:13:16,357
Cat

153
00:13:16,357 --> 00:13:20,637
Clara

154
00:13:24,157 --> 00:13:26,257
So this is what he's made of!

155
00:13:26,257 --> 00:13:27,957
My father's greatest rival.

156
00:13:27,957 --> 00:13:34,697
I... I won't lose.

157
00:13:36,737 --> 00:13:38,437
You got some fight left.

158
00:13:41,237 --> 00:13:44,137
Look, I'm not gonna kill you today, all right?

159
00:13:45,157 --> 00:13:48,537
Don't fight it. You're too valuable to die in a place like this.

160
00:13:48,677 --> 00:13:51,257
Run wild with us and our flag will be yours.

161
00:13:51,257 --> 00:13:58,497
And I will call you my son.

162
00:13:59,237 --> 00:14:01,097
Screw you, you old fart!

163
00:14:21,257 --> 00:14:50,257
Eh!

164
00:14:50,257 --> 00:14:53,997
Hey, I'm Whitebeard's 4th Division commander.

165
00:14:55,977 --> 00:14:57,477
The name's Thatch.

166
00:14:58,437 --> 00:14:59,837
If you're gonna join us,

167
00:15:00,837 --> 00:15:03,477
I'm a good friend to have.

168
00:15:03,657 --> 00:15:04,477
Shut up!

169
00:15:06,277 --> 00:15:08,317
Kind of grumpy when you wake up, huh?

170
00:15:09,317 --> 00:15:11,997
Oh, yeah, you're probably wondering what happened,

171
00:15:12,157 --> 00:15:13,437
since you passed out, I mean.

172
00:15:14,117 --> 00:15:17,157
Well, your crew proved their loyalty and came to get you back.

173
00:15:17,597 --> 00:15:19,617
So, of course, we beat the hell out of them.

174
00:15:20,257 --> 00:15:22,217
But they're not dead.

175
00:15:22,737 --> 00:15:23,997
They're all in the ship, too.

176
00:15:25,037 --> 00:15:26,837
Shouldn't I be in a cell or something?

177
00:15:27,057 --> 00:15:28,857
You don't even have shackles on me.

178
00:15:29,037 --> 00:15:30,877
Shackles? Nah, we don't need them.

179
00:15:31,077 --> 00:15:31,557
Not on you.

180
00:15:31,557 --> 00:15:54,877
Come on!

181
00:15:54,877 --> 00:15:56,557
You know what time it is!

182
00:15:56,557 --> 00:15:59,017
Yeah, we got people trying to sleep on this ship!

183
00:15:59,017 --> 00:16:15,257
Guys! He went overboard!

184
00:16:15,257 --> 00:16:16,717
I don't think he can swim!

185
00:16:16,717 --> 00:16:18,497
Hey, someone fish him out.

186
00:16:21,057 --> 00:16:22,717
He's been at it every day.

187
00:16:23,217 --> 00:16:25,017
Kid must be stuffed with guts.

188
00:16:26,677 --> 00:16:28,037
Does that make a hundred?

189
00:16:28,457 --> 00:16:29,577
I lost count.

190
00:16:29,577 --> 00:16:47,437
Tell me.

191
00:16:47,437 --> 00:16:51,917
Why does everyone on this ship call him Pops?

192
00:16:51,917 --> 00:16:55,697
You don't get it?

193
00:16:55,697 --> 00:16:58,637
Because he calls us sons.

194
00:16:59,777 --> 00:17:01,637
None of us have any family left.

195
00:17:01,717 --> 00:17:03,217
Hell, the whole world hates us.

196
00:17:03,957 --> 00:17:05,077
So it's nice, right?

197
00:17:05,577 --> 00:17:07,517
I mean, I know it's just a word.

198
00:17:08,057 --> 00:17:09,657
But it still feels nice.

199
00:17:09,657 --> 00:17:19,257
What's the deal?

200
00:17:19,577 --> 00:17:22,937
Are you really going to keep on doing this even after he's spared your life?

201
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:24,837
Because you can't keep this up.

202
00:17:26,357 --> 00:17:29,617
Hate to break it to you, but you're not strong enough to kill him.

203
00:17:29,617 --> 00:17:33,597
So you can either get off this ship and start over.

204
00:17:34,917 --> 00:17:36,437
Or you can stay here.

205
00:17:38,437 --> 00:17:41,097
And wear the mark of Whitebeard on your back.

206
00:17:49,097 --> 00:17:50,657
So, you must be Doma.

207
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:55,557
Whoa!

208
00:17:56,077 --> 00:17:57,977
Hot damn, Ace did it again!

209
00:17:57,977 --> 00:18:01,117
He got Doma and his crew to surrender all by himself!

210
00:18:01,577 --> 00:18:03,877
You guys want me to command the Second Division?

211
00:18:04,177 --> 00:18:06,917
The post has been open for a long time, so just take it.

212
00:18:07,197 --> 00:18:08,537
Yeah, nobody's going to complain.

213
00:18:11,217 --> 00:18:13,257
You're part of the original crew, right?

214
00:18:13,637 --> 00:18:15,137
This doesn't bother you at all?

215
00:18:17,077 --> 00:18:18,597
Nah, not in a slightest.

216
00:18:19,437 --> 00:18:21,877
I got no ambition for that sort of thing.

217
00:18:23,337 --> 00:18:26,457
Do it for us, Commander Ace.

218
00:18:27,977 --> 00:18:52,717
Hey, Pops, you got a minute?

219
00:18:52,717 --> 00:18:59,117
Well, damn.

220
00:18:59,397 --> 00:19:00,297
I'm surprised.

221
00:19:00,677 --> 00:19:01,937
I had no idea.

222
00:19:04,717 --> 00:19:07,737
Though, to be honest, you don't take after old Roger much.

223
00:19:08,737 --> 00:19:09,797
He was your enemy.

224
00:19:11,057 --> 00:19:12,477
Don't you want to kick me out?

225
00:19:12,697 --> 00:19:15,757
The look on your face, I thought you had something important to tell me.

226
00:19:15,977 --> 00:19:17,857
But I couldn't think of anything more trivial.

227
00:19:17,857 --> 00:19:20,597
I don't care where the hell you came from.

228
00:19:20,817 --> 00:19:22,517
We're all children of the sea.

229
00:19:22,517 --> 00:19:35,517
From this day forward, Ace will be our 2nd Division Commander!

230
00:19:35,517 --> 00:19:43,517
Don't look so dazed, buddy, you're a star, now eat!

231
00:19:52,517 --> 00:20:07,517
Here!

232
00:20:07,517 --> 00:20:11,517
Slow down, the food's not going anywhere, buddy, I promise you.

233
00:20:11,517 --> 00:20:17,517
Besides, the banquet today's in your honor.

234
00:20:17,517 --> 00:20:22,517
He fell asleep!

235
00:20:22,517 --> 00:20:26,517
Whitebeard's sure on a roll, he just picked up another strong rookie.

236
00:20:26,517 --> 00:20:32,517
I heard this new kid can breathe fire!

237
00:20:36,517 --> 00:20:41,517
Here comes the 2nd Division!

238
00:20:41,517 --> 00:20:42,517
Ace!

239
00:20:42,517 --> 00:20:44,517
You okay there, Thatch?

240
00:20:44,517 --> 00:20:46,517
Yep, I am now.

241
00:20:47,517 --> 00:20:53,517
Bet they'll raise your bounty again?

242
00:20:53,517 --> 00:20:54,517
Possibly.

243
00:20:54,517 --> 00:20:56,517
Ace, take a look at what I found.

244
00:20:56,517 --> 00:20:59,517
Oh, is that a devil fruit?

245
00:20:59,517 --> 00:21:02,517
I think so, but I don't know what type it is yet.

246
00:21:02,517 --> 00:21:11,517
Please, Ace, come on! Just calm down!

247
00:21:11,517 --> 00:21:14,517
Puff said he's gonna make an exception with this one! He doesn't want you going after Teach!

248
00:21:14,517 --> 00:21:23,517
Let me go! I'm his commander, aren't I? If I don't bring Teach to justice for this, how can Thatch's spirit ever rest?

249
00:21:23,517 --> 00:21:32,517
Ace, Ace, I know how you feel, but let it go. I've got a bad feeling about this one.

250
00:21:32,517 --> 00:21:41,517
The man killed his own crewmate and ran away! You've treated him like your son for decades now! Then he turns and spits in your face!

251
00:21:41,517 --> 00:21:50,517
He's disgraced my father's good name! I can't allow that! I'll take care of this on my own!

252
00:21:50,517 --> 00:22:08,517
Hey, hold on! Come back here, Ace!

253
00:22:08,517 --> 00:22:12,517
Hey, hold on! Come back here, Ace!

254
00:22:27,517 --> 00:22:29,517
Is the Koika over?

255
00:22:29,517 --> 00:22:32,517
Is that his power? Cause holy crap!

256
00:22:34,517 --> 00:22:35,517
Pops...

257
00:22:35,517 --> 00:22:39,517
Everyone else, too.

258
00:22:41,517 --> 00:22:44,517
I ignored your advice and took off on my own!

259
00:22:44,517 --> 00:22:47,517
Why the hell didn't you just give up on me?!

260
00:22:47,517 --> 00:22:49,517
Every bit of this is my own damn fault!

261
00:22:52,517 --> 00:22:53,517
